 "source": "Private Function One(s As Object, ByVal which As Long) As String\n    Dim v As Variant\n    On Error Resume Next\n    Select Case which\n    Case 0\n        v = s.Fill.Visible\n    Case 1\n        v = s.Fill.Type\n    Case 2\n        v = s.Fill.ForeColor.RGB\n    Case 3\n        v = s.Fill.ForeColor.ObjectThemeColor\n    Case 4\n        v = s.Fill.ForeColor.Type\n    Case 5\n        v = s.Fill.Transparency\n    Case 6\n        v = s.Fill.Pattern\n    Case 7\n        v = s.Line.Visible\n    Case 8\n        v = s.Line.ForeColor.RGB\n    Case 9\n        v = s.Line.ForeColor.ObjectThemeColor\n    Case 10\n        v = s.Line.Weight\n    Case 11\n        v = s.Line.DashStyle\n    Case 12\n        v = s.Line.Transparency\n    Case 13\n        v = s.Line.BeginArrowheadStyle\n    Case 14\n        v = s.Line.EndArrowheadStyle\n    Case 15\n        v = s.Shadow.Visible\n    End Select\n    If Err.Number Then\n        One = \"E\" & Err.Number\n    Else\n        One = CStr(v)\n    End If\nEnd Function\n\nPublic Function ReadShape(s As Object) As String\n    Dim i As Long, t As String\n    For i = 0 To 15\n        t = t & \"|\" & One(s, i)\n    Next\n    ReadShape = Mid$(t, 2)\nEnd Function\n\nPublic Function ReadAt(ByVal path As String, ByVal target As String) As String\n    Dim wb As Workbook\n    Application.DisplayAlerts = False\n    Set wb = Workbooks.Open(path, 0)\n    ReadAt = ReadShape(wb.Worksheets(1).Shapes(target))\n    wb.Close False\nEnd Function\n\nPrivate Sub Change(s As Object, ByVal which As Long)\n    Select Case which\n    Case 0\n        s.Fill.ForeColor.RGB = 255\n    Case 1\n        s.Fill.ForeColor.ObjectThemeColor = 6\n    Case 2\n        s.Fill.Visible = msoFalse\n    Case 3\n        s.Fill.Visible = msoTrue\n    Case 4\n        s.Fill.Transparency = 0.25\n    Case 5\n        s.Fill.Solid\n    Case 6\n        s.Fill.Patterned 5\n    Case 7\n        s.Line.ForeColor.RGB = 65280\n    Case 8\n        s.Line.ForeColor.ObjectThemeColor = 7\n    Case 9\n        s.Line.Visible = msoFalse\n    Case 10\n        s.Line.Visible = msoTrue\n    Case 11\n        s.Line.Weight = 4\n    Case 12\n        s.Line.DashStyle = 4\n    Case 13\n        s.Line.Transparency = 0.5\n    Case 14\n        s.Line.EndArrowheadStyle = 2\n    End Select\nEnd Sub\n\nPublic Function InModel(ByVal target As String, ByVal which As Long) As String\n    Dim t As String, s As Object\n    Set s = ActiveWorkbook.Worksheets(1).Shapes(target)\n    On Error Resume Next\n    Change s, which\n    t = \"E\" & Err.Number & \"@\"\n    Err.Clear\n    On Error GoTo 0\n    InModel = t & ReadShape(s)\nEnd Function\n",
